      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "So how can we add a gradient in the background here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 9.45,
          "en": "Well, for this we'll utilize expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.45,
          "end": 12.9,
          "en": "If you search for expo linear gradient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.9,
          "end": 14.77,
          "en": "you will find that expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.77,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "this extra tool we're using to simplify the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 20.36,
          "en": "of building React Native apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.36,
          "end": 23.61,
          "en": "this tool, and the team and company behind it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.61,
          "end": 27.46,
          "en": "provides an extra package called expo linear gradient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.46,
          "end": 29.64,
          "en": "that gives us a component, which we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.64,
          "end": 33.333,
          "en": "in our code to display a linear gradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.93,
          "end": 38.08,
          "en": "So, what we have to do here is open a new tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.08,
          "end": 39.65,
          "en": "in our terminal here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.65,
          "end": 42.73,
          "en": "so that we can install this extra package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.73,
          "end": 45.61,
          "en": "and we should install it with expo install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.61,
          "end": 49.38,
          "en": "not with npm install, you could do this as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.38,
          "end": 51.34,
          "en": "but by using expo install,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.34,
          "end": 53.62,
          "en": "expo, this tool which we're using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.62,
          "end": 56.7,
          "en": "will ensure that a fitting version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.7,
          "end": 58.98,
          "en": "is installed into this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.98,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "So it will take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 63.21,
          "en": "at the version of expo you are using in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "and it will automatically install a dependency version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 69.233,
          "en": "that works well with that expo version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.22,
          "end": 72.5,
          "en": "Therefore we'll use expo install here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.5,
          "end": 77.053,
          "en": "and install the expo-linear-gradient package like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.27,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "If you hit enter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 82.26,
          "en": "this will execute npm install behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.26,
          "end": 85.42,
          "en": "but as mentioned, it picks a fitting version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.42,
          "end": 88.89,
          "en": "Now, once it's done, you can close this terminal window",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 91.52,
          "en": "and keep the npm start process running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.52,
          "end": 95.4,
          "en": "And now we can import LinearGradient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 100.093,
          "en": "from expo linear gradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.36,
          "end": 104.34,
          "en": "And as always, the official docs are a great place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.34,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "to understand how you can use this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 108.18,
          "en": "in case you're not sure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.75999999999999,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "So now we imported this LinearGradient component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 115.38,
          "en": "And with that imported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.38,
          "end": 119.263,
          "en": "we can replace this view with LinearGradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 123.42,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, we can get rid of that view import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.42,
          "end": 125.51,
          "en": "because we're not using the view component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.51,
          "end": 127.263,
          "en": "in this app component anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.727,
          "end": 131.44,
          "en": "Now LinearGradient takes a style prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.44,
          "end": 134.68,
          "en": "and on that style, we still wanna set flex: 1 because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.68,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "the gradient also should take all the available space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 141.47,
          "en": "but we won't set a background color anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.47,
          "end": 143.14,
          "en": "because the idea behind that gradient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.14,
          "end": 146.183,
          "en": "is that we have a gradient between multiple colors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.02,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "And we set those multiple colors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "with help of the colors prop that is supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 155.393,
          "en": "by this LinearGradient component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.27,
          "end": 158.71,
          "en": "This colors prop takes an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.71,
          "end": 162.61,
          "en": "which takes all the colors you want to use in your gradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.61,
          "end": 164.42000000000002,
          "en": "That could be two colors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.42000000000002,
          "end": 166.5,
          "en": "It could be five colors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.5,
          "end": 169.15,
          "en": "Again, take a look at the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.15,
          "end": 171.84,
          "en": "to learn more about all these supported properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.84,
          "end": 173.973,
          "en": "and how you can configure this gradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.04,
          "end": 179.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now, the two colors I want to use here are, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.17000000000002,
          "end": 182.56,
          "en": "the yellow, which we used for the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.56,
          "end": 183.993,
          "en": "so I will pick this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 188.69,
          "en": "But as a first color, I want to use a different color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.69,
          "end": 191.5,
          "en": "I want to use this plum color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.5,
          "end": 195.61,
          "en": "which I used for the background of my input container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.61,
          "end": 198.38,
          "en": "So I will grab this as a first color here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.38,
          "end": 201.44,
          "en": "separate these items with a comma,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.44,
          "end": 204.2,
          "en": "and with that, if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.2,
          "end": 207.86,
          "en": "you have this nice gradient here in the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.86,
          "end": 209.57999999999998,
          "en": "Of course, with that added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.57999999999998,
          "end": 213.06,
          "en": "to make sure that there is a higher contrast",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.06,
          "end": 215.32,
          "en": "between the background and this container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.32,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "this input container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 219.27,
          "en": "we could go back to this container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.27,
          "end": 224.267,
          "en": "and pick a even darker plum color here, like 3b021f.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 227.19,
          "end": 229.56,
          "en": "And with that now this is darker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.56,
          "end": 232.69,
          "en": "and stands out more from the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.69,
          "end": 235.43,
          "en": "But this is how we can add a gradient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.43,
          "end": 238.34,
          "en": "And thanks to this extra expo package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.34,
